Z||000003||b lo 0||08-04-2000||02:48 PM||||Is it just me or has Ferrari gotten really REALLY concieted lately?  Like no one can put a rearing horse on a yellow background without them suing the ****  out of them.  Sorry about the language, but this is one of those issues that has always gotten under my skin.  That's why I will NEVER EVER build a Ferrari replica or buy a Ferrari (also I can't afford one).  I collect Matchbox and Hot Wheels cars.  I have about 400 models, and only one is a Ferrari, a model my best friend gave me for a christmas stocking stuffer.  I refuse to buy anything that even resembles a Ferrari, so that way I don't inflate their already bloated egos.  You can't even get onto their website <A HREF="http://www.ferrari.it" TARGET=_blank>www.ferrari.it</A>  without being a registered loser I mean user.  I guess if you buy one they give you a logon name and password.  OK, i'm finished rambling.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">      <BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.i-p.com" TARGET=_blank>www.audioimagery.i-p.com</A>  !!!<P><A HREF="http://clubs.excite.com/welcome/main?cid=.zXb1DJ1lsCL&aid=22&auth=" TARGET=_blank>Pontiac Fiero Owner's Club</A>-Pics, Videos and More-Or Post your Own<p>[This message has been edited by b lo 0 (edited 08-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||mshill||08-04-2000||04:41 PM||||For this exact reason I am going to have my own emblems and ornaments made for my Fiero-50 when completed.  Yep, a yellow shield with the Fiero Pegasus on it.  I am also going to see is I can get a Chromed Pegasus ornament made for the front and rear grills.  It will look like an F-50 but will have Fiero all over it!||||reg||1
